      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy develops higher friction as temperature approaches 800 °C.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11355469::rubric_card::000::5a35f0b817"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy develops higher wear rates at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Uncontrolled, nonprotective oxide formation causes the elevated-temperature friction and wear of the starting alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is addition of approximately 3–5 at.% Cu to CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Added Cu segregates to the sliding interface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfacial Cu promotes formation of a fine, nanocrystalline Cu-rich oxide layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cu-doped regions preferentially oxidize during sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preferential oxidation produces a continuous, adherent, lubricious Cu-rich oxide film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, the Cu-rich film remains sufficiently thin that it does not adversely affect friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At higher temperatures, the Cu-rich oxide film becomes thicker while remaining well adhered.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature Cu-rich oxide film reduces interfacial shear stress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high-temperature Cu-rich oxide film resists abrasive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 3–5 at.% Cu will yield lower coefficients of friction than undoped CoCrFeNi throughout 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 3–5 at.% Cu will yield lower wear rates than undoped CoCrFeNi throughout 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted benefit is bounded to sliding in ambient air at loads on the order of 1 N and temperatures from 25 °C to 800 °C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A pin-on-disk comparison at 25 °C, 400 °C, and 800 °C can measure friction, wear, and Cu-rich oxide formation in doped and undoped specimens.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
